                <pb facs="0320" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-01T10:00:00-04:00">September 1,
                            1939—10 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>163. Your 279, August 31, 5 p.m. Please inform Aranha that the American Chargé
                    d’Affaires in La Paz has been instructed to continue normal relations with the
                    present Bolivian Government. No question of recognition has been raised by this
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
